e.", "support_note": "Confidence score logs document the missed events.", "support_status": "weakly_supported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2029A", "claim": "Device confidence scores confirm the failure.", "support_note": "Confidence score logs document the missed events.", "support_status": "weakly_supported"}], "confidence": 0.75, "evidence_links": [], "missing_evidence": ["At least one retrieved technical artifact supporting the incident judgment.", "Clinical SHACL nonconformance requires human review."], "rationale": "The device failed to flag a clinically significant ventricular tachycardia episode in real time, with confirmed recurrence across the deployed population (SYNTHETIC NARRATIVE). This represents a realized serious patient-safety risk, as missed detection of ventricular tachycardia can lead to severe harm or death. The confirmation of recurrence establishes a broad deployed-population exposure to this risk.  The device's failure to perform its intended function requires review under EU MDR Annex I, Section 17.1 regarding electronic programmable systems and their repeatability, reliability, and performance (mdr-annexI-sec17.1-electronic-programmable). The software development lifecycle must be reviewed in accordance with the state of the art, including risk management and verification/validation (mdr-annexI-sec17.2-software-lifecycle).  The incident also triggers obligations under 21 CFR \u00a7 820.10(c) concerning design controls for devices automated with computer software (qmsr-820.10-c-design-development), specifically related to ISO 13485 clause 7.3. The device's IT security measures also require review, as a failure in the classifier could be linked to unauthorized access or other vulnerabilities (mdr-annexI-sec17.4-it-security).  The device confidence-score logs for both missed episodes (ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2025A, ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2029A) confirm the failure and provide data for investigation.", "recommendation": "ESCALATE_TO_HUMAN_IMMEDIATE", "requires_human_review": true, "severity": 4}, "final_report_sha256": "dc3438ee34525c5639c43b8b474e96e6bf7e8874461172945781cbf9e3c05a2f", "generation_source": "ollama_real", "invalid_proposals": 0, "is_fallback": false, "is_mock": false, "opa_actions": ["severity4_or_death_forced_immediate_human_escalation", "technical_incident_missing_technical_evidence", "deny:technical_incident_missing_technical_evidence", "clinical_shacl_nonconformance_routes_review"], "recommendation": "ESCALATE_TO_HUMAN_IMMEDIATE", "record_type": "terminal", "report_id": "SYN-IND-0029", "retrievals": 1, "revisions": 0, "run_id": "inloop_SYN-IND-0029_df181406", "scenario_id": "SYN-IND-0029", "schema_version": "2.1.0", "severity": 4, "shacl_findings": [{"message": "RiskReport must link at least one evidence id.", "severity": "Severity: sh:Violation", "shape": "shacl"}], "state_terminal": "terminal", "termination_reason": "human escalation or invalid transition", "timestamp_utc": "2026-08-06T09:06:48.780136Z", "total_steps": 5, "trace_id": "6184bafe-497f-4916-92ed-56299f0add78"}
